# Verified-inapplicable ChromaDB advisories, not blind suppressions - see
# each entry for why. Re-check this file whenever chromadb is upgraded.
#
# chromadb==0.4.22 is pinned (see requirements.txt's comment: newer
# chromadb needs NumPy 2.x, this app pins NumPy <2.0). Both CVEs below are
# in chromadb's SERVER (its FastAPI app: multi-tenant auth, the
# authenticated HTTP API). This app never runs that server or exposes it
# on a network - every usage is `chromadb.PersistentClient(...)` (grep
# confirms: only PersistentClient appears anywhere in app/), an embedded,
# in-process, single-tenant local client with no HTTP listener and no
# concept of "authenticated users" at all. Neither is reachable in this
# deployment. (A third, related advisory - CVE-2026-45829, pre-auth code
# injection on the same server - exists upstream for chromadb but Trivy
# doesn't flag it against this exact pinned version; not suppressed here
# since it was never actually reported.)

# ChromaDB: code injection vulnerability (chromadb's HTTP server). No
# fixed version listed upstream as of this scan.
CVE-2026-45833

# ChromaDB: authenticated users can read/write/delete any tenant's
# collection (chromadb's HTTP server multi-tenant authorization). No
# fixed version listed upstream as of this scan.
CVE-2026-45830
